          ":question/id": "b653b8c3-f330-53fd-9729-fc5cdad2a545",
          ":question/math-academy-id": "q-131305",
          ":question/problem": "What are the pivot columns of the matrix $P,$ given by\n\n$$\nP=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 & 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 0 & -2 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply.",
          ":question/worked-solution": "First, we need to convert $P$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 & 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 0 & -2 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 & 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 0 & -2 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{4} & :={R}_{4}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 & 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLooking at the row echelon form, we see that $P$ has $3$ pivots. In particular, the pivot columns are the $1$st, $3$rd, and $5$th columns."
